{
  "text": "Pick any positive number. If it is even, divide by two. If it is odd, multiply by three and add one. This is the 3x plus 1 problem, also known as the Collatz Conjecture. No matter what number you start with, every single one seems to collapse down to four, two, one. Yet despite supercomputer checks up to quintillions, nobody has been able to prove it mathematically. Paul Erd\u0151s famously said mathematics is simply not yet ready for such problems.",
